0..79 Comment "// Univalence over the user universe, after the HoTT book\'s § 2.10 and cubical"
80..146 Comment "// Agda\'s `Cubical/Foundations/Univalence.agda`. `ua(e)` makes the"
147..216 Comment "// bi-invertible map `e : A ≃ B` between two types of `Type` a path"
217..297 Comment "// `Path(Type, A, B)`, admitted on the record\'s two laws as its evidence, at any"
298..372 Comment "// two codes: two variables, or a path type and a presented type, which no"
373..450 Comment "// finite round-trip coverage reaches. Transport along it applies the map, by"
451..528 Comment "// conversion (cubical\'s `uaβ`) and by a run. Transport along a path between"
529..600 Comment "// types, packaged as the record, is `idtoequiv` (the book\'s `idtoeqv`,"
601..678 Comment "// cubical\'s `pathToEquiv`); `ua` and `idtoequiv` make a quasi-inverse and so"
679..753 Comment "// an equivalence, `univalence`, on two owed laws: `ua` after `idtoequiv`,"
754..833 Comment "// which no rule converts, and `idtoequiv` after `ua`, which needs the record\'s"
834..874 Comment "// inverses to be determined by its map."
875..877 Comment "//"
878..919 Comment "// - see: #650 — `oneBack`, `idtoequiv`"
920..950 Comment "// - see: #695 — `idtoequiv`"
951..981 Comment "// - see: #698 — `idtoequiv`"
982..1024 Comment "// - see: #1979 — `loopsAreTheirWinding`"
1025..1051 Comment "// - see: #520 — `uaEta`"
1052..1083 Comment "// - see: #656 — `univalence`"
1085..1156 Comment "// The circle, the presented integers, the winding number and spinning."
